### B1. `CLS-PII-CC-001` — 0 matches on `test_file.pdf` (3 occurrences of the card)
**Root cause confirmed: the separator class `[- ]?` admits exactly one character, and only hyphen or space — never a newline, and never two whitespace chars.**

| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |
|---|---|---|
| `Visa 4532-\n8910-4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[5,25]` |
| `4532-8910-4321-9081` | match `[0,19]` | match `[0,19]` |
| `4532-\n8910-\n4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[0,21]` |
| `4532  8910  4321  9081` (double spaces) | **no match** | match |
| `4532-\n\n8910-4321-9081` (blank line) | no match | **no match** (guard holds) |
| `order 1234\n5678\n9012` (12 digits) | no match | no match |
| `ref 2026\n1016` (date-like) | no match | no match |
| `3782 822463 10005` (Amex 4-6-5, 15 digit) | no match | **no match — out of scope, see risk R1** |

**Corrected separator class requirement:** must accept `hyphen`, spaces/tabs (runs of any length), and **at most one newline** per separator, but must **not** allow a blank line (which would let a match bridge two unrelated paragraphs).

**Corrected pattern (validated):**
```json
"pattern": "\\b(?:\\d{4}(?:[ \\t\\-]*\\n?[ \\t\\-]*)){3}\\d{4}\\b"
```
Human-readable: `\b(?:\d{4}(?:[ \t\-]*\n?[ \t\-]*)){3}\d{4}\b`

**Luhn post-validator (new `validators` block) — and the conflict:**
```
luhn(digits):
  digits = [int(c) for c in re.sub(r'\D','',match)]
  return (sum(digits[-1::-2]) + sum(sum(divmod(2*d,10)) for d in digits[-2::-2])) % 10 == 0
