| `mavance_admin` (no label) | **no match** — proves context anchoring |
| `user marcus.vance@example.com` | **no match** |
| `Account mavance_admin` (no colon) | **no match** |

In the document's own text the same construct yields **`mavance_admin` at `[83,96]`** (the synthetic probe string yields 9–22 purely because of a shorter prefix).

**Floor question, resolved:** (i) rev-001 has no global floor, so no *technical* exception is needed; (ii) the proposed **0.86 / threshold 0.85 is justified by the label anchoring** (label + colon is a mandatory, non-optional lookbehind, which is what makes the difference between ~0.75 naive precision and ≥0.85); (iii) **Admin decision D-3:** either accept 0.86/0.85 as specified, **or** if Admin elects to codify a *global PII floor = 0.85* as a new schema field, this classifier already complies. **No 0.75 variant is proposed.**
